    "CAST demonstrated higher rates of mortality or nonfatal cardiac arrest in post-MI patients treated with encainide or flecainide when used to suppress PVCs and NSVT. Propafenone is associated with increased mortality in SCA survivors compared with beta blockers, amiodarone, and the ICD. Implantation of an ICD prior to achieving suppression of frequent or incessant VA places the patient at high risk of repetitive shocks, related to increased mortality. Sustained monomorphic VT post-MI is typically scar-related. Revascularization is unlikely to reduce monomorphic VT. Cardiac MRI is useful for NICM diagnosis and assessing SCA/SCD risk. Genetic counseling/testing is suggested for those under 40 with NICM or LV dysfunction with family history. Delayed hyperenhancement, associated with scar and worse outcomes, links to VA. It is important to consider genetic etiologies for NICM, with genetic counseling helping clarify prognosis.": "content"
